 ## Verified Facts
 
 - `TripViewBeta.loadAndPresent` accepts `HybridIdentifier`, forwarding UUID or folio lookups through `getTrip` and constructing the detail from the returned response. Trip-list and followup selections pass `.id(item.id)`; status callbacks continue to use the loaded trip's concrete UUID.
-- `TripViewBeta` reserves a 35px status action row below its right-side data grid. Pending trips expose Iniciar Viaje and Cancelar Viaje; in-progress trips expose Completar Viaje and Cancelar Viaje; terminal states expose neither. Start/complete actions use the shared green crystal modifier and cancel uses red, with matching hover/focus accents and a dimmed disabled state. `ConfirmTripStatusUpdate` gathers the typed transition, a trimmed comment (required for cancellation), and `ChangeTripStatusMedia` grouped by fiscal merchandise item ID. Its source uses the existing unregistered `.asset` image-upload/camera pipeline, correlates each completion to a row/event, keeps the first completed image as avatar, and blocks confirmation until pending uploads/camera requests finish or are cancelled. Removal aborts local uploads and ignores late responses. Before presentation/submission, asset merchandise requires unique linked store/warehouse/subaccount origin and destination snapshots; media requires unique trip-merchandise IDs and safe image basenames. The server remains authoritative for actual asset state and tenant records. The beta `changeStatus` method submits the trip ID, requested status, comment and media through the typed wrapper. Status actions are disabled while the request is pending. Only a successful API response changes the local trip/status and calls the parent status callback; a guarded getTrip refresh loads the new status/comment notes, while failed requests retain the prior status. Responses from a changed session are ignored, while successful responses still notify the parent if the detail was closed. These facts were verified in source; browser/upload behavior remains unverified.
